{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#2281","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#2281","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#2281\",\"parent_revision\":\"c6d27b824f730f57f8dd0e88ac63be53528429912192ee131c9ee3e64f7edea0\",\"root_revision\":\"c6d27b824f730f57f8dd0e88ac63be53528429912192ee131c9ee3e64f7edea0\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: \\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: closed\\nadded: \\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nThe start-task skill's documented invocation format is `{task_file_path} --task {task_id}`, which requires the caller to supply a filesystem path to the plan YAML file. This path is an internal implementation detail of the SAM backend \u2014 it should never be visible at the skill interface level.\\n\\nThe SAM MCP server already resolves plan addresses: `sam_plan(action=status, plan=\\\"Pdec8934d\\\")` and `sam_plan(action=read, plan=\\\"Pdec8934d\\\")` both work with the address alone. The file path is available internally via the `source_path` field in the read response.\\n\\nThe correct interface is `{plan_address} --task {task_id}` (e.g. `Pdec8934d --task T01`), with start-task resolving the plan internally via MCP rather than accepting a caller-supplied path.\\n\\nSecondary unknown: whether start-task currently passes the path argument to the SAM MCP (making this a doc+interface bug) or reads the YAML file directly (making it a code bug as well). Needs to be verified by reading the start-task skill implementation.\\n\\nSupersedes #2280 (closed \u2014 was logged at P1 in error).\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer relying on this plugin**, I want to **start-task skill requires filesystem path \u2014 plan address should be sufficient** so that **the tool works correctly and reliably**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Observed during /dh:implement-feature Pdec8934d \u2014 orchestrator had to call sam_plan(action=read) and extract source_path to obtain the file path required by start-task args. User confirmed P0.\\n- **Priority**: P0\\n- **Added**: 2026-05-15\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\\n## Groomed (2026-05-16)\\n\\n### Reproducibility\\n\\n1. Open any session where `/dh:implement-feature` is active for a plan (e.g. `Pdec8934d`).\\n2. Observe the orchestrator call `sam_plan(action=read, plan=\\\"Pdec8934d\\\")` to obtain `source_path` from the response.\\n3. Observe the orchestrator then pass `source_path` as the first argument to `Skill(skill=\\\"start-task\\\", args=\\\"{source_path} --task T01\\\")`.\\n4. The extra `sam_plan(read)` call to extract the path is the observable waste \u2014 the orchestrator should not need it.\\n\\n### Output / Evidence\\n\\n- Orchestrator transcript for plan `Pdec8934d` shows a `sam_plan(action=read)` call whose only purpose is extracting `source_path` to satisfy the `start-task` interface.\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/start-task/SKILL.md` line 4: `argument-hint: <task-file-path> [--task <task-id>] [--complete <task-id>]` \u2014 documents a filesystem path requirement.\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/implement-feature/SKILL.md` line 111: `Skill(skill=\\\"start-task\\\", args=\\\"{task_file_path} --task {task_id}\\\")` \u2014 caller template uses `task_file_path`.\\n- `plugins/development-harness/agents/task-worker.md` line 51: `Skill(skill=\\\"start-task\\\", args=\\\"{plan} --task {task_id}\\\")` \u2014 already uses plan address form (inconsistency with implement-feature).\\n- `plugins/development-harness/docs/backlog-item-lifecycle.md` lines 447, 476: Mermaid diagram and state table both use `task_file_path`.\\n- `plugins/development-harness/docs/workflow-architecture-diagram.md` line 398: hook parse comment still references `<path>` pattern.\\n\\n### Priority\\n\\nP0 \u2014 Observed live during `Pdec8934d` session. Every `implement-feature` invocation wastes an extra `sam_plan(read)` call and exposes an internal implementation detail to all callers. `task-worker.md` already uses the correct address form, creating inconsistency across the skill surface.\\n\\n### Impact\\n\\n- Blocks: Every orchestrator running `/dh:implement-feature` is forced to do an extra `sam_plan(read)` just to extract `source_path` to satisfy the interface \u2014 wasted MCP round-trip.\\n- Bottleneck: All task dispatch in the SAM pipeline passes through this interface. The mismatch propagates to `implement-feature`, `backlog-item-lifecycle.md`, `workflow-architecture-diagram.md`, `task_status_hook.py` regex patterns, and any caller documentation that references the path-based form.\\n\\n### Benefits\\n\\n- Removes the extra `sam_plan(action=read)` call from every implement-feature dispatch loop iteration.\\n- Eliminates filesystem-path leakage at the skill interface boundary \u2014 callers need only the plan address, which is already known from `sam_plan(action=ready)`.\\n- Makes `start-task`, `implement-feature`, `task-worker`, lifecycle docs, and the hook consistent on address-form arguments.\\n- Aligns with the existing `task-worker.md` which already uses `{plan} --task {task_id}` (address form) \u2014 brings `implement-feature/SKILL.md` in sync.\\n\\n### Expected Behavior\\n\\nWhen an orchestrator has a plan address (e.g. `Pdec8934d`) and a task ID (e.g. `T01`), it calls `Skill(skill=\\\"start-task\\\", args=\\\"Pdec8934d --task T01\\\")` directly. The skill resolves all plan context via MCP internally using the address. No filesystem path is required or visible at the invocation boundary.\\n\\n### Desired Structure\\n\\n- `start-task/SKILL.md` argument-hint: `<plan_address> [--task <task-id>] [--complete <task-id>]`\\n- `start-task/SKILL.md` Parse Arguments section: `plan_address` (required), not `task_file_path`\\n- `implement-feature/SKILL.md` dispatch template: `Skill(skill=\\\"start-task\\\", args=\\\"{plan_address} --task {task_id}\\\")`\\n- `task-worker.md` example: already correct (`{plan} --task {task_id}`) \u2014 no change needed\\n- `backlog-item-lifecycle.md` Mermaid diagram and state table: replace `task_file_path` with `plan_address`\\n- `workflow-architecture-diagram.md` hook parse comment (line 398): replace `<path>` with `<plan_address>`\\n- `task_status_hook.py` regex patterns (lines 259 and 268\u2013273): accept `P[0-9a-f]+` address tokens in addition to `.md|.yaml` file extensions; context file may store `plan_address` instead of `task_file_path`\\n- `complete-implementation` references: verify whether `complete-implementation` also accepts a path and apply same fix if so\\n\\n### Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n1. `start-task/SKILL.md` argument-hint contains `<plan_address>`, not `<task-file-path>`.\\n2. The Parse Arguments section in `start-task/SKILL.md` documents `plan_address` as the first positional argument.\\n3. `implement-feature/SKILL.md` dispatch template calls `Skill(skill=\\\"start-task\\\", args=\\\"{plan_address} --task {task_id}\\\")` \u2014 not `{task_file_path}`.\\n4. `backlog-item-lifecycle.md` Mermaid diagram and state table no longer reference `task_file_path` in the start-task dispatch nodes.\\n5. `workflow-architecture-diagram.md` hook parse documentation references plan address pattern, not file path.\\n6. `task_status_hook.py` regex patterns successfully parse `P[0-9a-f]+` address tokens from Skill invocation args (verified by existing or new unit tests in `tests/test_task_status_hook.py`).\\n7. Running `uv run pytest plugins/development-harness/tests/test_task_status_hook.py -x` passes with no failures.\\n8. `complete-implementation/SKILL.md` is inspected; if it also accepts a path as its first argument, the same fix is applied.\\n\\n### Resources\\n\\n| Type | Item |\\n|------|------|\\n| Skill (subject) | /dh:start-task \u2014 `plugins/development-harness/skills/start-task/SKILL.md` |\\n| Skill (caller) | /dh:implement-feature \u2014 `plugins/development-harness/skills/implement-feature/SKILL.md` |\\n| Skill (inspect) | /dh:complete-implementation \u2014 inspect for same path bug in its first argument |\\n| Agent (already correct) | `plugins/development-harness/agents/task-worker.md` \u2014 already uses address form |\\n| Hook script | `plugins/development-harness/skills/implementation-manager/scripts/task_status_hook.py` \u2014 regex at lines 259, 268\u2013273 |\\n| Hook tests | `plugins/development-harness/tests/test_task_status_hook.py` \u2014 `_extract_plan_addr_from_path` and `extract_task_info_from_prompt` |\\n| Doc (lifecycle) | `plugins/development-harness/docs/backlog-item-lifecycle.md` \u2014 lines 447, 466, 476, 509 |\\n| Doc (architecture) | `plugins/development-harness/docs/workflow-architecture-diagram.md` \u2014 line 398 |\\n\\n### Dependencies\\n\\n- Depends on: None \u2014 all artifacts are in the local codebase, no external blockers.\\n- Blocks: #2282 (implement-feature commit ownership) and #2283 (swarm-task-planner commit step) \u2014 both touch `implement-feature/SKILL.md` and would produce merge conflicts if landed after this fix. This fix should land first or the three be coordinated in the same branch.\\n\\n### Blockers\\n\\nNone \u2014 the secondary unknown from the description is resolved. Reading `start-task/SKILL.md` confirms the skill does NOT read the YAML file directly. It uses MCP address form (`plan=\\\"P{N}\\\"`) in all internal calls. The filesystem path is only stored in the hook context file and parsed by `task_status_hook.py`. The fix scope is: interface documentation + hook regex patterns + test coverage.\\n\\n### Effort\\n\\nSmall \u2014 the skill body already uses address form internally. Changes are confined to: the argument-hint line and Parse Arguments section in `start-task/SKILL.md`, one dispatch template line in `implement-feature/SKILL.md`, two documentation files (`backlog-item-lifecycle.md`, `workflow-architecture-diagram.md`), and regex patterns in `task_status_hook.py` plus corresponding test coverage in `test_task_status_hook.py`.\\n\",\"digest\":\"b65405af8737615870dc339d162a73b1314efce7eed59a9a27db43c5df0fec12\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABVCTW-Q\"}"}